---
import Landing from '../../layouts/Landing.astro';
---

<Landing title="Where to Be When Supply Chains Break" description="Bolivia as a resilience hedge. Crisis analysis, safety data, and why physical community beats financial instruments.">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="min-h-screen flex items-center bg-bark-900 text-bark-300 px-6 lg:px-10 pt-16">
    <div class="max-w-[900px] mx-auto py-20">
      <span class="text-label text-accent reveal">Resilience</span>
      <h1 class="text-display text-bark-50 mt-6 reveal" data-delay="100">
        The grid is a bet.<br/>What's your hedge?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-bark-400 mt-8 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="200">
        A cooperative in the Bolivian cloud forest learning to provision its own
        power, food, water, and governance -- in a place where those things are
        still possible to build from scratch.
      </p>
      <div class="accent-line max-w-xs mt-12 reveal" data-delay="300"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Key stats -->
  <section class="section-gap px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1100px] mx-auto">
      <span class="text-label text-bark-500 reveal">The Numbers</span>
      <h2 class="text-headline text-bark-800 mt-4 mb-12 reveal" data-delay="100">
        Bolivia ranked #7 of 17 countries analyzed
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        <div class="card hover-lift reveal" data-delay="100">
          <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="stat-value text-accent">#7</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Overall crisis safety rank</div>
            <div class="stat-context">Out of 17 countries assessed across 6 disruption scenarios</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card hover-lift reveal" data-delay="200">
          <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="stat-value">0</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Nuclear targets</div>
            <div class="stat-context">No nuclear weapons, no reactors, no strategic military installations</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card hover-lift reveal" data-delay="300">
          <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="stat-value">4.4</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Homicides per 100K</div>
            <div class="stat-context">Lower than the US (6.4) and most of Latin America</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card hover-lift reveal" data-delay="400">
          <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="stat-value">1,750m</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Altitude at Coroico</div>
            <div class="stat-context">Year-round food production, 18-28C, no heating or cooling needed</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider-accent max-w-[1100px] mx-auto"></div>

  <!-- The thesis -->
  <section class="section-gap px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="content-width">
      <span class="text-label text-bark-500 reveal">The Thesis</span>
      <h2 class="text-headline text-bark-800 mt-4 mb-8 reveal" data-delay="100">
        Physical community beats financial instruments
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-6 text-body-lg text-bark-600 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <p>
          When supply chains fracture, the value of a productive community with its own food, energy,
          and manufacturing capacity exceeds any portfolio of financial derivatives designed to hedge
          the same risks. The hedge is the community itself.
        </p>
        <p>
          Bolivia offers structural advantages that cannot be replicated in the Global North:
          low cost of land, legal frameworks for cooperative ownership by foreigners,
          food sovereignty at altitude, and geographic distance from the conflict zones
          that dominate most disruption scenarios.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Yungas cloud forest at 1,750 meters provides year-round growing seasons,
          abundant water from Andean springs, and a climate that requires neither heating
          nor air conditioning -- the two largest energy costs in most settlements.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section-gap-lg px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="content-width text-center">
      <h2 class="text-headline text-bark-800 mb-8 reveal">
        Decide for yourself.
      </h2>
      <a href="/en/resilience" class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 px-8 py-4 bg-accent text-white font-display font-semibold text-sm tracking-wide rounded-full hover:bg-accent-dim transition-colors duration-300 reveal" data-delay="100">
        See the crisis data and methodology
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Honest disclaimer -- placed after CTA to preserve momentum -->
  <section class="section-gap bg-bark-100 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="content-width text-center">
      <div class="tag tag-accent mb-6 mx-auto reveal">Honest Disclosure</div>
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-6 reveal" data-delay="100">
        This is a research initiative, not a finished product.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-bark-500 max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal" data-delay="200">
        No land has been purchased. No legal entity exists. No one is selling you
        safety. We are publishing our analysis, building our models in the open,
        and inviting scrutiny. The crisis data is real. The community is forming.
        The rest is work ahead.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Landing>
